{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527933-some-w5-plot-ideas","id":1527933,"title":"Some W5 plot ideas","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-01-04T11:05:47-08:00","id":1527933,"title":"Some W5 plot ideas","content":"As much as I am critical of W5, it does offer an unique chance to really play with the different factions and roles in the game. So here are some plots for people to use.<br /> <br /> (NOTE: CoF and Harano/Hauglosk are not mentioned, I want to focus on the tribes and BSDs in this.)<br /> <br /> <b>1. Hey, that was ours!</b><br /> A very likely Kin the pack has been watching suddenly goes missing, their tracks end at the local Red Talon pack's territory. The Kin is found . . . consumed. When the Talons are called out on this, they point out that the Kin was a human born and so not as valuable as a wolf-born, besides the PC pack had once declared the Litany was no longer needed so what's the issue? Will the PC pack avenge the Kin?<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>2. Bad Neighbours</b><br /> A new Caern has been created near the PC pack's territory. What seemed like a pleasant surprise is turned into horror as the Caern is guarded by a large pack of BSDs. The alpha of the pack offers the PC pack alpha a deal; Gaia is dead so there is no reason to fight each other. The BSDs will leave the PC pack alone if the PC pack leaves the BSDs alone. Will the PCs accept the deal? Or will they risk a costly fight and a potential loss of territory?<br /> <br /> <b>3. Guilty by Association</b><br /> The pack finds themselves suddenly hunted by a cell of hunters. Unwilling to kill humans who seem like good people, the pack tries to offer peace. The hunters refuse, declaring that all werewolves are sexual predators, cannibals and torturers. It seems the only garou the hunters met have been BSDs. Will the PCs try to clear their name and risk revealing too much?<br /> <br /> <b>4. Getting the Band Back Together</b><br /> Enough is enough, the territory is too big for one pack to handle and there aren't enough hours in the day to address every concern the spirits have. The pack decides to form a sept to ease their burden and ensure the Caern stays safe. But are they prepared to handle all the politics running a sept involves?<br /> <br /> <b>5. Utopia?</b><br /> The local Silver Fang packs has decided to pool all their resources together and create a garou-only city. They invite the PC pack to join them. When asked how to keep the city free of humans, the Fang alpha says there are 'methods.'<br /> <br /> <b>6. Damaged Goods</b><br /> A serial killer stalking an area near the pack turns out to be Kin. Now the pack is left with an awkward choice; Kill them, let the BSDs take them or try to convince them to join a Gaian tribe?<br /> <br /> <b>7. They are a bit confused.</b><br /> A Stolen Moon has contacted the pack, wishing to join. By all respects, they seem genuine in their wish and their ritual did not involve killing werewolves. Are they worth the risk, will the pack Patron even accept them? Or is there something more sinister afoot?<br /> <br /> <b>8. You got my cover in YOUR cover!</b><br /> A gang the pack is part of starts losing members as a new task force at the local precinct is frighteningly effective at their job. Turns out, they too are a pack of werewolves. The cop pack asks the PC pack to think beyond their human ties and consider what is best for Gaia. Will the PCs tell them to shove it?<br /> <br /> <b>9. Later Phases</b><br /> The alpha of an allied pack announces their retirement from werewolf life. They plan to lose the wolf and focus on their touchstones full-time. But losing their skills would be a shame...<br /> <br /> <b>10. The Village 2: Electric Boogaloo!</b><br /> A Touchstone of one of the pack visits their family in the countryside and doesn't return. When the pack investigates, they find an isolated village openly being ruled by a pack of tribeless garou. They tell the PC pack to leave and find their own herd to feed on. Is fighting them the best choice? What about the humans, including the Touchstone, who now know of the garou?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-05T04:38:30-08:00","id":1528011,"title":"","content":"I was debating doing a 101 Adventure Hooks for Werewolf 5 but wasn't sure if I had enough of a grasp on the setting yet to distinguish it from previous editions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-05T12:27:59-08:00","id":1528045,"title":"","content":"All of these seem to be plots that could have been used in previous editions of the game. Many in fact are either plots I've run as ST, prepared to run only not to use, or seen other STs do in some format (meaning the general idea, not necessarily the specifics laid out here). The only partial exemption is #2 with the &quot;Gaia is dead argument&quot;, though it'd be easy to come up with some other rationale a BSD pack might offer a PC pack that they leave each other alone. So while these may be good plots for W5, I don't see any unique opportunities the W5 setting offers that previous editions of the setting did not. Revised had a tendency to treat the setting as white hat good guys coming together in a high fantasy feel, but the OG 1e setting had lots of understandable conflicts between Garou and more conflicted NPCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-05T12:54:53-08:00","id":1528049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527933-some-w5-plot-ideas?p=1528045#post1528045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All of these seem to be plots that could have been used in previous editions of the game. Many in fact are either plots I've run as ST, prepared to run only not to use, or seen other STs do in some format (meaning the general idea, not necessarily the specifics laid out here). The only partial exemption is #2 with the &quot;Gaia is dead argument&quot;, though it'd be easy to come up with some other rationale a BSD pack might offer a PC pack that they leave each other alone. So while these may be good plots for W5, I don't see any unique opportunities the W5 setting offers that previous editions of the setting did not. Revised had a tendency to treat the setting as white hat good guys coming together in a high fantasy feel, but the OG 1e setting had lots of understandable conflicts between Garou and more conflicted NPCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>To me, the difference lies in the fact that there is no longer any oversight or a larger nation. Even in 1st ed, there was still a clear society of garou around and you could not do just whatever.<br /> <br /> In W5, there is no one but your pack and some allies to fight the wyrm OR not fight the Wyrm and just live in the caern. The Litany is no longer respected by all, so you end up with garou who aren't even corncerned about anything beyond feeding themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-17T04:14:04-08:00","id":1528706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527933-some-w5-plot-ideas#post1527933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As much as I am critical of W5, it does offer an unique chance to really play with the different factions and roles in the game. So here are some plots for people to use.<br /> <br /> (NOTE: CoF and Harano/Hauglosk are not mentioned, I want to focus on the tribes and BSDs in this.)<br /> <br /> <b>1. Hey, that was ours!</b><br /> A very likely Kin the pack has been watching suddenly goes missing, their tracks end at the local Red Talon pack's territory. The Kin is found . . . consumed. When the Talons are called out on this, they point out that the Kin was a human born and so not as valuable as a wolf-born, besides the PC pack had once declared the Litany was no longer needed so what's the issue? Will the PC pack avenge the Kin?</div> </div> </div> </div>This could happen in the original version, just not as openly and even without the litany or the act of devouring, it doesn't change the fact that they killed an ally of yours. By the way, does it have to be Red Talons? Couldn't it be any pack of wolfborn that would be the same?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527933-some-w5-plot-ideas#post1527933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>3. Guilty by Association</b><br /> The pack finds themselves suddenly hunted by a cell of hunters. Unwilling to kill humans who seem like good people, the pack tries to offer peace. The hunters refuse, declaring that all werewolves are sexual predators, cannibals and torturers. It seems the only garou the hunters met have been BSDs. Will the PCs try to clear their name and risk revealing too much?</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, this could happen in the original format. Unless it was a group you have no hope of winning.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527933-some-w5-plot-ideas#post1527933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>4. Getting the Band Back Together</b><br /> Enough is enough, the territory is too big for one pack to handle and there aren't enough hours in the day to address every concern the spirits have. The pack decides to form a sept to ease their burden and ensure the Caern stays safe. But are they prepared to handle all the politics running a sept involves?</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, this could happen in the original format.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527933-some-w5-plot-ideas#post1527933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>5. Utopia?</b><br /> The local Silver Fang packs has decided to pool all their resources together and create a garou-only city. They invite the PC pack to join them. When asked how to keep the city free of humans, the Fang alpha says there are 'methods.'</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it would work in the original format if you switched to ronins, or skindancers or just dissidents.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527933-some-w5-plot-ideas#post1527933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>6. Damaged Goods</b><br /> A serial killer stalking an area near the pack turns out to be Kin. Now the pack is left with an awkward choice; Kill them, let the BSDs take them or try to convince them to join a Gaian tribe?</div> </div> </div> </div>This one could, no doubt. He's simply a lost orphan.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527933-some-w5-plot-ideas#post1527933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>7. They are a bit confused.</b><br /> A Stolen Moon has contacted the pack, wishing to join. By all respects, they seem genuine in their wish and their ritual did not involve killing werewolves. Are they worth the risk, will the pack Patron even accept them? Or is there something more sinister afoot?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you exchange Stolen Moon for a dancing ronin I believe it could be done in the original material. It would require a certain suspension of disbelief, but it could.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527933-some-w5-plot-ideas#post1527933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>8. You got my cover in YOUR cover!</b><br /> A gang the pack is part of starts losing members as a new task force at the local precinct is frighteningly effective at their job. Turns out, they too are a pack of werewolves. The cop pack asks the PC pack to think beyond their human ties and consider what is best for Gaia. Will the PCs tell them to shove it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if I understand this one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527933-some-w5-plot-ideas#post1527933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>9. Later Phases</b><br /> The alpha of an allied pack announces their retirement from werewolf life. They plan to lose the wolf and focus on their touchstones full-time. But losing their skills would be a shame...</div> </div> </div> </div>It's literally a Garou wanting to retire, I believe that in both formats it wouldn't make a difference. Unless the Garou nation has a rule against retirement that I didn't know about and if the objective is to survive... if he could just stay with his family why didn't he just stay from the beginning? Missing information?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527933-some-w5-plot-ideas#post1527933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>10. The Village 2: Electric Boogaloo!</b><br /> A Touchstone of one of the pack visits their family in the countryside and doesn't return. When the pack investigates, they find an isolated village openly being ruled by a pack of tribeless garou. They tell the PC pack to leave and find their own herd to feed on. Is fighting them the best choice? What about the humans, including the Touchstone, who now know of the garou?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-17T07:28:31-08:00","id":1528712,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27832_1.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27832\" data-vbnamecard=\"27832\">Psicose</a> A lot of the examples couldn't have happened, because the larger Nation would have offered another solution. Red Talons keep their man-eating hidden in previous versions but in W5 they don't have to.<br /> <br /> The chance of the hunters running first into BSDs is possible but not as likely as in W5. The BSDs in previous versions are hiding far harder than in W5.<br /> <br /> I don't know how decentralized the Nation is in your games, but Getting The Band Back Together is about there being no larger Nation that could arrange this by default. Caern creation gives a lot of renown, so there would be plenty of other garou to help the pack. Plus, older versions have a set structure that W5 lacks.<br /> <br /> In general, garou in older versions do not retire. They fight until they are so infirm they perform the Rite of Winter Wolf, which is a ritualized suicide. Simply losing the wolf and retiring wouldn't happen, since the garou would feel obligation to the war effort. In W5, there is no greater war effort.<br /> <br /> Most of these ideas rely on the players being the highest authority around with no one higher to give them marching orders. So their choices will be different just from the lack of resources that other editions have.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-17T07:43:14-08:00","id":1528713,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27832_1.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27832\" data-vbnamecard=\"27832\">Psicose</a><br /> <br /> I'm confued about your complaints. It's the next edition of the game. What does saying, &quot;It could have happened in W1-20&quot; contribute to the thread other than threadcrapping?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-17T08:32:11-08:00","id":1528716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/we